ies, generates, transmits, distributes, and sells electric energy in the United States. It owns and operates coal-fired, natural gas-fired, wind-powered, and solar-powered generating assets. The company also provides retail electric services to approximately 913,000 customers that covers a service area of approximately 30,000 square miles. Additionally, it offers bill payment and electric construction services for residential and business sectors. OGE Energy Corp. was founded in 1902 and is based in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Sean Trauschke | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers. Each employee generates $37K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["OGE Energy Corp is a large-cap utilities business with a $10.7B market cap on $3.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 42%.","The business throws off $83M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 42% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4249077453869504},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Financial quality scores above most Utilities peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing OGE Energy (NYSE:OGE) and Evergy (NASDAQ:EVRG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/reviewing-oge-energy-nyseoge-and-evergy-nasdaqevrg.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794359708.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.952,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Raised Earnings Guidance Will Impact OGE Energy Stock Investors","s